==Welsh==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|cy|myned||literary}}

===Etymology===
Suppletive verb:
* Verbal noun from {{inh|cy|wlm|mynet}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*moned}} (compare {{cog|kw|mones}}, {{cog|br|mont}}, {{cog|cel-gau|moni|t=come!}}), verbal noun of {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*monītor}} (compare {{cog|mga|muinithir||goes around}}), from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*menH-}} (compare {{cog|xum|menes||will come}}, {{cog|lt|mìnti||to trample, scutch}}).<ref>{{R:cel:EDPC|page=276}}</ref>
* Indicative forms from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ageti||to drive}} (compare {{cog|sga|aigid}}), from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (compare {{cog|la|agō}}).
* The forms in ''el-'' are from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ɸalnati||to approach, drive}}, from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*pelh₂-}} (compare {{cog|la|pellō||strike, drive}}, {{cog|grc-epc|πίλναμαι||approach}}.
* The origins of imperative forms {{m|cy|dos}} and {{m|cy|cer}} remain unexplained.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/mɨ̞nd/|a=cy-N,standard,colloquial}}
** {{IPA|cy|/mɨ̞n/|a=cy-N,colloquial}}
* {{IPA|cy|/mɪnd/|a=cy-S,standard,colloquial}}
** {{IPA|cy|/mɪn/|a=cy-S,colloquial}}
* {{rhymes|cy|ɨ̞nd|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{cy-verb|1s=af|irr=1}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{ux|cy|Mae hi'n '''mynd''' i Gaerdydd heno.|inline=1|t=She's '''going''' to Cardiff tonight.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Aeth''' hi ddoe.|inline=1|t=She '''went''' yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Awn''' ni edrych.|inline=1|t=We '''will go''' and look.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Ait''' ti i'r ysgol ar droed.|inline=1|t=You '''used to go''' to school on foot.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Mae'n angenrheidiol yr '''elwyf''' nawr.|inline=1|t=It is necessary that I '''go''' now.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Na, rwy'n '''mynd''' ar y trên bach.|t=No, I'm '''going''' on the little train.|inline=1}}
# to [[become]]
#: {{ux|cy|'''Aeth''' hi wallgof.|inline=1|t=She '''went''' insane.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Mae Sioned yn '''mynd''' yn grac.|inline=1|t=Sioned is getting ['''going'''] angry.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Mae'r peth 'ma wedi '''mynd''' yn wyrdd.|inline=1|t=This thing has '''gone''' green.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Af''' i grac.|inline=1|t=I will get ['''go'''] angry.}}

